# Component & Project Architecture

## Directory Structure
```
├── app/         # Pages, layouts, routes (Server Components by default)
├── components/  # UI atoms and complex organisms
├── hooks/       # Extracted client-side logic
├── utils/       # Helpers and formatters
└── types/       # Global TypeScript contracts
```

## Rules
- **Single responsibility:** small, focused components — no 500-line monoliths.
- **Server-first:** keep components as Server Components; add `"use client"` only when
  interactivity/state/effects are required, and isolate that to the smallest leaf.
- **Logic in hooks:** extract data fetching, state machines and side effects into `hooks/`.
- **Dynamic import** heavy client-only components to protect Core Web Vitals.
- **No prop drilling chaos:** compose, or use context for genuinely shared state only.
